[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114437,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "<p >Squamous odontogenic tumour (SOT) is a benign epithelial odontogenic tumour with squamous differentiation.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-10T17:04:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114438,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9312/0 Squamous odontogenic tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114439,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E83.0 &amp; XH4PV9 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of skull or face &amp; Squamous odontogenic tumour</p>\r\n<p>2E83.1 &amp; XH4PV9 Benign osteogenic tumours of bone or articular cartilage of lower jaw &amp; Squamous odontogenic tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114440,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114441,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114442,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOT affects the tooth-bearing parts of the jaws. Most are solitary lesions with a predilection for the anterior maxilla and posterior mandible. Multifocal and peripheral SOTs have been reported {2674829; 8515987; 27632187}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114443,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOT usually present as an asymptomatic swelling. A minority are associated with pain, tenderness, mobility of teeth, or bone expansion.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>SOT typically presents as a triangular or semicircular unilocular radiolucency with well-defined borders along one or more tooth roots. Cortication of margins is variable. Root displacement is common, but root resorption is rare. Cortical bone perforation is seen in less common multilocular and aggressive lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114444,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The mean age at diagnosis is 34.8&nbsp;years, with an almost equal prevalence in men and women {29311021; 32717216}. Multifocal SOTs tend to present in a younger age group and show a marked predilection for African Americans {27632187}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114445,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown, but a familial incidence has been reported {2674829; 33246182}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114446,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A role for NOTCH receptors and their ligands in the cytodifferentiation of SOT has been proposed {20554499}, and mutations in <em>AMBN</em> have been found {15288841}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114447,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most SOTs are submitted as tan-grey or brown curettings of soft tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114448,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SOT comprises variably sized and shaped islands of cytologically bland well-differentiated squamous epithelium in a fibrous or myxoid stroma. The peripheral cells of the islands are flat to cuboidal, with very infrequent mitoses. The central cells have a tendency for cystic degeneration, individual cell keratinization, and calcification. Mucous metaplasia, sebaceous differentiation, and ghost cell&ndash;like areas may be present as minor changes {27632187; 32717216}. SOT does not exhibit peripheral palisading, reverse nuclear polarity, cellular atypia, or pleomorphism.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The entities should include acanthomatous ameloblastoma, desmoplastic ameloblastoma, and well-differentiated squamous cell carcinoma. SOT-like proliferation of epithelium may develop in the lining of odontogenic cysts and is a close histological mimic of SOT {285403}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114449,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 139,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-28T10:23:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
